# REQUIRES: verilator
# Serialized links between SLR groups (`--slr-serialize [<glob>:]<k>`): the
# producer's group holds the bits of its pass and sends a k-th of them a host
# cycle over the k after the next, every chunk from the held bits (no logic of
# the pass in front of the crossing register), the reader's group shifts them
# back together and writes the link k + 1 host cycles after the pass; the
# producer's passes of a kind stay k apart. A crossing takes a k-th of the wires. Exact against the
# target, channels stalled or not, with bubbles, early and late links.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linkpage
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/s2 --static --nest --modulo --slr-groups --slr-count 2 --slr-assign Unit:0,Reader:1,Top_model:1 --slr-serialize 2 Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=S2
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=S2SIM < %t/s2/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/s2/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/s2/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/s2/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/s2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/s2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/b --static --nest --modulo --bubbles --slr-groups --slr-count 2 --slr-assign Unit:0,Reader:1,Top_model:1 --slr-serialize Unit:4,Reader:2 Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIX
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/b/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/b/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/b/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/b/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +bubble=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/b/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +bubble=50 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/b/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +bubble=30 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# Late links (zero latency within a group), a chain over three groups.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/late
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/l3 --static --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-count 3 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-serialize 3 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/l3/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/l3/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/l3/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/l3/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/l3/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=40 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/l2 --static --copies Leaf:3 --two-cycle-links --slr-groups --slr-count 2 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:0,Top_model:1 --slr-serialize Leaf*:2 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/l2/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/l2/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/l2/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/l2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# S2: II = 10
# S2: slr links serialized: 48 wires for 96 bits
# S2: Unit -> Reader: 1 links, 32 bits, 2 host cycles on 16 wires
# S2SIM: hw.module private @foldsim_sim_slr0({{.*}}out Unit_out_slr1_0 : i16)
# S2SIM: %Unit_out_slr1_0_hold = seq.compreg.ce
# MIX: Unit -> Reader: 1 links, 32 bits, 4 host cycles on 8 wires
# MIX: Reader -> Unit: 1 links, 32 bits, 2 host cycles on 16 wires
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
